egin searching for Facebook repos. I'll use the provided function. After that, I'll need to plan further actions to find and fork Facebook repos, but for this act(), I'll just navigate to explore projects as the first step.\n</reasoning>\n\n<code>\nasync def act(page):\n    # Use the knowledge base function to navigate to explore projects\n    await navigate_to_explore_projects(page)\n</code>\n\n<exception>\n'TimeoutError': Locator.click: Timeout 5000ms exceeded.\nCall log:\n  - waiting for get_by_role(\"link\", name=\"Explore projects\", exact=True)\n    - locator resolved to <a href=\"/explore\" data-placement=\"right\">Explore projects\u21b5</a>\n  - attempting click action\n</exception>\n\n---\n\n<reasoning>\nI need to fork all repos from Facebook. I'm currently on the GitLab dashboard page after a failed attempt to navigate to explore projects due to a timeout. The accessibility tree shows the dashboard with various projects, but none appear to be from Facebook (e.g., no 'facebook' in names). I need to find Facebook repos first. Since the previous action failed with a TimeoutError when trying to click 'Explore projects', I should try a different approach. Looking at the tree, I see a link 'Explore projects' with URL '/explore'. I can directly navigate to that URL using page.goto('/explore') instead of relying on the function that might have timing issues. After navigating to explore projects, I can search for Facebook repos. The knowledge base function navigate_to_explore_projects is disabled as per the note, so I cannot use it. I'll use relative navigation to '/explore'. This is a new action from the current state. After this navigation, I'll need to plan further actions to find and fork Facebook repos, but for this act(), I'll just navigate to explore projects as the next step.\n</reasoning>\n\n<code>\nasync def act(page):\n    # Navigate to explore projects page directly using relative URL\n    await page.goto('/explore')\n    # Wait for the page to load\n  